Package: vdstreamer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: vd-streamer-linux <noreply@localhost>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://www.vrdesktop.net
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, zlib1g, libssl3 | libssl3t64 | libssl1.1, ca-certificates,
 libgstreamer1.0-0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly | gstreamer1.0-openh264, gstreamer1.0-x, gstreamer1.0-pipewire,
 libpulse0, pulseaudio-utils, libx11-6, libxrandr2, systemd
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal, wl-clipboard | xclip, libnotify-bin, gstreamer1.0-vaapi | gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad,
 ffmpeg, libavcodec61 | libavcodec-extra61
Suggests: yt-dlp
Description: Virtual Desktop Streamer for Linux (unofficial port)
 Streams the Linux desktop, audio and microphone to the Virtual Desktop app on
 Meta Quest, Pico and other headsets, with keyboard/mouse/controller input.
 .
 Reuses the Virtual Desktop protocol libraries from the official macOS streamer
 (proprietary, Virtual Desktop, Inc.) with a native Linux capture/encode/input
 layer (PipeWire portal or X11, GStreamer NVENC/VA-API/x264, PulseAudio/PipeWire,
 uinput). Not affiliated with or supported by Virtual Desktop, Inc.
